   "notes": "Tail of the 'Suffixes' entry begun at the foot of col. 2 on p. 752, which broke after '863 a 2, 9, 17,'; the opening 'b 8' therefore inherits section 863. Three bare numbers in the runs of suffix subsections are 20 or more — '22, 23' after '861. 11, 19', and '21' after '863 a 8, 12, 16' — so the contract's under-20 test would make them plain sections. They are recorded here as inherited subsection anchors and flagged uncertain: Smyth's suffix lists in 861 and 863 run past 20 items, and §§21-23 of the grammar (consonant classification) have nothing to do with suffixes. The print also uses a comma, not a semicolon, before 'material' and before 'fitness'.",
